dn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2400x1350+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Ff4%2F8f%2F920ee85049b19c94d1dce98d8815%2F6-images.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2400x1350+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Ff4%2F8f%2F920ee85049b19c94d1dce98d8815%2F6-images.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2400x1350+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Ff4%2F8f%2F920ee85049b19c94d1dce98d8815%2F6-images.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2400x1350+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Ff4%2F8f%2F920ee85049b19c94d1dce98d8815%2F6-images.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2400x1350+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Ff4%2F8f%2F920ee85049b19c94d1dce98d8815%2F6-images.jpg" class="img" alt="Clockwise from left, East of Eden, Neagley, Brothers, A Different World, Slow Horses and Cupertino." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Clockwise from left, &lt;em&gt;East of Eden, Neagley, Brothers, A Different World, Slow Horses&lt;/em&gt; and &lt;em&gt;Cupertino.&lt;/em&gt;                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Geoffrey Short/Netflix; Sabrina Lantos/Prime; Apple TV; Daniel Delgado Jr/Netflix; Apple TV; Elizabeth Fisher/CBS                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;b class="toggle-caption"&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/b&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Check out what &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/sections/culture/" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NPR&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;strong&gt; is watching, reading and listening to this weekend:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🍿 Movies:&lt;/strong&gt; NPR's &lt;em&gt;Pop Culture Happy Hour&lt;/em&gt; describes &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/08/nx-s1-5955757/filipinana-is-not-your-average-eat-the-rich-tale" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Filipiñana&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt; as visually beautiful and an emotional gut punch, offering a fresh take on the inner workings of a Philippines' country club.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;📺 TV:&lt;/strong&gt; Florence Pugh in an &lt;em&gt;East of Eden&lt;/em&gt; adaptation, a reboot of &lt;em&gt;A Different World,&lt;/em&gt; and Matthew McConaughey and Woody Harrelson playing (possible) brothers are among the anticipated shows coming this fall. Here's &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/10/nx-s1-5902184/what-to-watch-new-tv" target="_blank"&gt;what NPR critics are looking forward to&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;📚 Books:&lt;/strong&gt; In Colin Kaepernick's new memoir, &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/09/nx-s1-5791621/colin-kaepernick-perilous-fight-jay-z-nfl-deal" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;em&gt;The Perilous Fight&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, he reflects on his life, going back even further than a decade ago when he famously took a knee. &lt;a href="https://one.npr.org/i/nx-s1-5791621:x" target="_blank"&gt;In an interview with &lt;em&gt;Morning Edition&lt;/em&gt;'s Michel Martin&lt;/a&gt;, he discusses losing his football career and what the protest taught him.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🎵 Music:&lt;/strong&gt; NPR's &lt;em&gt;New Music Friday &lt;/em&gt;is sharing the best albums out this week, including Ezra Collective's &lt;em&gt;Here Because of Hope &lt;/em&gt;and This Is Lorelei's &lt;em&gt;The Singer in My Band&lt;/em&gt;. Listen to several albums' &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/11/nx-s1-5963873/new-music-friday-the-best-albums-out-sept-11-2026" target="_blank"&gt;best songs with this curated playlist&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🧩 Games:&lt;/strong&gt; Want to cut down on doomscrolling? Check out these &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/05/nx-s1-5953957/daily-puzzle-games-history-geography" target="_blank"&gt;five daily puzzle games&lt;/a&gt; that will test your knowledge of geography, history and even obscure corners of Wikipedia.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;❓ Quiz:&lt;/strong&gt; What is better than one quiz? Two! You are destined to get at least one &lt;a href="http://npr.org/2026/09/11/g-s1-142657/will-you-get-5-000-to-do-the-news-quiz-no-but-will-it-be-fun-maybe" target="_blank"&gt;NPR news quiz&lt;/a&gt; question right if you know what big promise the president made this week. And, see how much you really know about procrastination with &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/06/nx-s1-5957512/quiz-ugh-ill-do-it-later-how-much-do-you-know-about-procrastination" target="_blank"&gt;this &lt;em&gt;Life Kit &lt;/em&gt;quiz&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;3 things to know before you go&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-142745" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 7060;         --source-height: 3971;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7060x3971+3126+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6e%2Fa2%2F86b79eed4041a812789ac1a341d4%2Ffull-feather-200x.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7060x3971+3126+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6e%2Fa2%2F86b79eed4041a812789ac1a341d4%2Ffull-feather-200x.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7060x3971+3126+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6e%2Fa2%2F86b79eed4041a812789ac1a341d4%2Ffull-feather-200x.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7060x3971+3126+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6e%2Fa2%2F86b79eed4041a812789ac1a341d4%2Ffull-feather-200x.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7060x3971+3126+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6e%2Fa2%2F86b79eed4041a812789ac1a341d4%2Ffull-feather-200x.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7060x3971+3126+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6e%2Fa2%2F86b79eed4041a812789ac1a341d4%2Ffull-feather-200x.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7060x3971+3126+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6e%2Fa2%2F86b79eed4041a812789ac1a341d4%2Ffull-feather-200x.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7060x3971+3126+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6e%2Fa2%2F86b79eed4041a812789ac1a341d4%2Ffull-feather-200x.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7060x3971+3126+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6e%2Fa2%2F86b79eed4041a812789ac1a341d4%2Ffull-feather-200x.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7060x3971+3126+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6e%2Fa2%2F86b79eed4041a812789ac1a341d4%2Ffull-feather-200x.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7060x3971+3126+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6e%2Fa2%2F86b79eed4041a812789ac1a341d4%2Ffull-feather-200x.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7060x3971+3126+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6e%2Fa2%2F86b79eed4041a812789ac1a341d4%2Ffull-feather-200x.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7060x3971+3126+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6e%2Fa2%2F86b79eed4041a812789ac1a341d4%2Ffull-feather-200x.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7060x3971+3126+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6e%2Fa2%2F86b79eed4041a812789ac1a341d4%2Ffull-feather-200x.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7060x3971+3126+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6e%2Fa2%2F86b79eed4041a812789ac1a341d4%2Ffull-feather-200x.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7060x3971+3126+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6e%2Fa2%2F86b79eed4041a812789ac1a341d4%2Ffull-feather-200x.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7060x3971+3126+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6e%2Fa2%2F86b79eed4041a812789ac1a341d4%2Ffull-feather-200x.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7060x3971+3126+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6e%2Fa2%2F86b79eed4041a812789ac1a341d4%2Ffull-feather-200x.jpg" class="img" alt="This fossilized feather dates back 66 million years to the late Cretaceous. “It is, without a doubt, the best feather we’ve ever found from the age of dinosaurs,” says Jingmai O’Connor, an associate curator at the Field Museum of Natural History." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 This fossilized feather dates back 66 million years to the late Cretaceous. "It is, without a doubt, the best feather we've ever found from the age of dinosaurs," says Jingmai O'Connor, an associate curator at the Field Museum of Natural History.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Nate Carroll&lt;br&gt;                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;b class="toggle-caption"&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/b&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;ol class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;Researchers say that a well-preserved fossil feather may help &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/10/nx-s1-5963519/best-fossilized-bird-feather-dinosaur-feces-extinction" target="_blank"&gt;explain why some birds survived&lt;/a&gt; the giant dinosaur-killing asteroid that struck Earth, while others did not.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;For the first time in 900 years, the &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/09/nx-s1-5891555/bayeux-tapestry-british-museum-opening" target="_blank"&gt;230-foot Bayeux Tapestry&lt;/a&gt; is back in England. It depicts the pivotal Battle of Hastings in 1066, marking the end of Anglo-Saxon rule.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The Herbie Hancock Institute of Jazz has selected &lt;a href="https://www.wrti.org/arts-desk/2026-09-10/11-young-singers-selected-for-the-herbie-hancock-jazz-competition" target="_blank"&gt;11 young singers as semifinalists&lt;/a&gt; for its International Jazz Vocals Competition. This year's event is the most internationally diverse in nearly four decades, with six vocalists from outside the United States. (via &lt;a href="https://www.wrti.org" target="_blank"&gt;WRTI&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This newsletter was edited by &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/1155154221/majd-al-waheidi"target="_blank"   &gt;&lt;em&gt;Majd Al-Waheidi&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
